  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────
  // T-885 (2026-11-17). `TODOS.md` part two items 57 and 68: the option VALUE rule is read from the record
  // that declares the parameter, instead of one 120-character single-line grammar for every family. The
  // operator chose this shape on 2026-11-17 ("Record-gated value rule", filed v0.1.0). The measured fault is
  // item 57-s own: a 300-character `options.lyrics` never reached the wire (ap-1648, and again ap-1647), the
  // row carried only the length, and the engine answered its own "MiniMax Music 3 requires lyrics". Item 68
  // measured the same gap from the bar side on 2026-11-16: the refusal quoted a record that said "structure
  // tags such as [verse] and [chorus] are supported" while this lane could not put a bracket on the wire.
  // THE INPUT IS THE ENGINE-S OWN PAGE AGAIN, for the same reason T-877 used it: the record that decides
  // these cases is not a shape written for the test. It declares `lyrics` as a required string with NO length
